was performed on day 50. Most of the lesions had disappeared, but ill-defined high-signal lesions remained in the periventricular and subcortical white matter and in the cortex. T2*-weighted gradient-echo MRI showed numerous punctate low-signal lesions in the centrum semiovale, subcortical white matter, periventricular white matter, and corpus callosum. T2WI: T2-weighted imaging, FLAIR: fluid-attenuated inversion recovery.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jcn-4-164-g002"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>